.TH HTTP_RESPONSE_DUMP 3
.SH NAME
http_response_dump \- print a response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "void http_response_dump(http_response* " r ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_response_dump ()
writes the transfer, status, header length, content length and multipart boundary of the response to standard error.
It does nothing unless the library was built with DEBUG_HTTP.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_dump(3)
